{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "scriptId": "pl-06-mixtures-weighted-cost",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Mixtures and Weighted Cost in Profit Problems",
    "description": "Combine goods bought at different rates, find the true mean cost, and set a selling rate for a target profit.",
    "teachingApproach": "Build weighted mean from total rupees over total quantity, then attach profit to the mean. Introduce alligation only after reverse-profit reasoning establishes the required mean cost, and finish with missing-component blend questions.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 28,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 12, Profit and Loss. Approved scope: Teach weighted cost per unit for mixtures: total cost divided by total quantity. Cover two and three purchase rates, equal-quantity traps, ratio-weighted mixtures, selling a blend at a target profit, recovering an unknown component cost, and using alligation only after converting a desired selling price back to the required mean cost. Include milk/water or tea/rice style commercial mixtures when the key skill is profit on the blend. Keep this lesson focused on cost weighting rather than general mixture theory."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn mixtures and weighted cost in profit problems.\n\nA grocer mixes 20 kg of rice at ₹30 per kg with 30 kg at ₹40. The mixture does not cost the simple average ₹35 — the larger lot must count more.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "When goods bought at different rates are mixed, the true cost per kg is a weighted average: add total rupees first, then divide by total kilograms.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "20 kg at ₹30 costs ₹600.\n30 kg at ₹40 costs ₹1200.\nTotal 50 kg costs ₹1800.\nMean C.P. = 1800/50 = ₹36/kg.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
        "text": "10 kg at ₹24/kg is mixed with 30 kg at ₹32/kg. Mean C.P. per kg?",
